    "lawCode": "Rpld §661 sub 6 ¶d, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4464\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to repeal paragraph d of subdivision 6 of section 661 of the\neducation law relating to the ban on incarcerated persons for receiving\nstudent financial aid awards\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill repeals the ban on incarcerated persons receiving student\nfinancial aid awards.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 repeals paragraph d of subdivision 6 of Section 661 of the\nEducation Law.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUntil 1995, incarcerated persons at state correctional facilities were\neligible to receive Tuition Assistance Program awards in order to pursue\nhigher education. In the interest of reducing recidivism, such awards\nshould be made available to those inmates who wish to use their period\nof incarceration to pursue their education and thereby better their\nchances to reenter society as productive, law-abiding citizens.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: S.790 - Referred to Higher Education/A.3975 - Referred to\nHigher Education\n2017-2018: S.3735 - Referred to Higher Education/A.3995 - Referred to\nHigher Education\n2015-2016: S.975 - Referred to Higher Education/A.2870 - Referred to\nHigher Education\n2013-2014: S.1367 - Referred to Higher Education/A.3401 - Referred to\nHigher Education\n2011-2012: S.369 - Committee Discharged and Committed to Rules/A.3837 -\nReferred to Higher Education\n2009-2010: S.1288 - Referred to Higher Education\n2007-2008: S.4085 Referred to Education/A.7043- Held For Consideration\nin Higher Education\n2005-2006: S.1480 Referred to Higher Education/A.2756 Referred to Higher\nEducation\n2003-2004: S.1630 Referred to Higher Education/A.2160 - Referred to\nHigher Education\n2001-2002: S.1045- Referred to Higher Education/A.1289 - Referred to\nHigher Education\n1999-2000: S.6664 - Referred to Higher/A.9608 - Referred to Ways and\nMeans\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
